{
  "area": "formula-formats",
  "about": "The format a Formula gives a General cell when it is entered (ADR-0047, second round). Microsoft does not document the rule for any function ExSheet declares (it does for DATE, TODAY and NOW, which ExSheet does not have), so the engine applies only what these cases have observed Excel to do: simple arithmetic (single-cell References, constants, + and -, parentheses) takes the format of the first formatted cell it reads, except that a date minus a date gives none; MIN and MAX over References take the format of their first formatted argument; anything else gives none. It applies only when the cell's format is General, and only when the Formula is entered. The uncertain cases record the engine's answer where Excel has not been asked.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "FF-001",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "A date plus a number shows as a date",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=A1+7"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"value2": 46298, "text": "10/3/2026", "numberFormat": "m/d/yyyy"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-002",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "A number plus a date shows as a date: the first formatted Reference, not the first operand",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=7+A1"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "10/3/2026", "numberFormat": "m/d/yyyy"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-003",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "A date minus a date is a number of days, and gives no format",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026", "A2": "9/20/2026"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=A1-A2"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"value2": 6, "text": "6", "numberFormat": "General"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-004",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "A Formula that is one Reference takes that cell's format",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=A1"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "9/26/2026", "numberFormat": "m/d/yyyy"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-005",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "A negated Reference in parentheses takes that cell's format",
      "cells": {"A1": "12.5%"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=-(A1)+1"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "87.50%", "numberFormat": "0.00%"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-006",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "The first Reference whose cell is formatted gives the format, an unformatted one before it passed over",
      "cells": {"A1": "5", "A2": "10%"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=A1+A2"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "510%", "numberFormat": "0%"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-007",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "A cell formatted before the Formula is entered keeps its format",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026"},
      "action": [
        {"do": "format", "range": "B1", "format": "0.00"},
        {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=A1+1"}}
      ],
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "46292.00", "numberFormat": "0.00"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-008",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "The format is taken once, at entry: formatting the cell read afterwards does not change it",
      "cells": {"A1": "5"},
      "action": [
        {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=A1+1"}},
        {"do": "format", "range": "A1", "format": "0.00"}
      ],
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "6", "numberFormat": "General"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-009",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "A cell read in a formatted column gives the column's format",
      "cells": {"A5": "3"},
      "action": [
        {"do": "format", "range": "A:A", "format": "0.00"},
        {"do": "enter", "cells": {"C5": "=A5+1"}}
      ],
      "check": "C5",
      "expect": {"text": "4.00", "numberFormat": "0.00"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-010",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "A Formula pasted as text takes a format as a typed one does",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026"},
      "action": {"do": "pasteText", "rows": [["=A1+1"]], "at": "B1"},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "9/27/2026", "numberFormat": "m/d/yyyy"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-011",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "Multiplication gives no format",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=A1*1"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "46291", "numberFormat": "General"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-012",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "MAX over dates takes the date format",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026", "A2": "9/27/2026"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=MAX(A1:A2)"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "9/27/2026", "numberFormat": "m/d/yyyy"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-013",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "A mixed expression is not simple arithmetic and gives no format",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=A1+2*3"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "46297", "numberFormat": "General"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-014",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "Text joined with & gives no format",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=A1&\"\""}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"value2": "46291", "kind": "text", "numberFormat": "General"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-015",
      "source": "observed",
      "description": "Arithmetic on General cells alone gives no format",
      "cells": {"A1": "5", "A2": "6"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=A1+A2"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "11", "numberFormat": "General"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-016",
      "source": "uncertain",
      "description": "Engine's answer, Excel to be asked: a date minus a number is a date",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=A1-7"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "9/19/2026", "numberFormat": "m/d/yyyy"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-017",
      "source": "uncertain",
      "description": "Engine's answer, Excel to be asked: MIN over dates takes the date format",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026", "A2": "9/20/2026"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=MIN(A1:A2)"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "9/20/2026", "numberFormat": "m/d/yyyy"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-018",
      "source": "uncertain",
      "description": "Engine's answer, Excel to be asked: MAX over dates plus a number takes the date format",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026", "A2": "9/20/2026"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=MAX(A1:A2)+1"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "9/27/2026", "numberFormat": "m/d/yyyy"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-019",
      "source": "uncertain",
      "description": "Engine's answer, Excel to be asked: MAX takes the format of its first formatted argument, an unformatted one before it passed over",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026", "C1": "5"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=MAX(C1,A1)"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "9/26/2026", "numberFormat": "m/d/yyyy"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-020",
      "source": "uncertain",
      "description": "Engine's answer, Excel to be asked: SUM over dates gives no format",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026", "A2": "9/20/2026"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=SUM(A1:A2)"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "92576", "numberFormat": "General"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-021",
      "source": "uncertain",
      "description": "Engine's answer, Excel to be asked: a date minus a date plus a number gives no format: the difference is days, and the number is General",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026", "A2": "9/20/2026", "A3": "7"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=A1-A2+A3"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"text": "13", "numberFormat": "General"}
    },
    {
      "id": "FF-022",
      "source": "uncertain",
      "description": "Engine's answer, Excel to be asked: a date minus a date formatted as a percentage is a date",
      "cells": {"A1": "9/26/2026", "A2": "10%"},
      "action": {"do": "enter", "cells": {"B1": "=A1-A2"}},
      "check": "B1",
      "expect": {"numberFormat": "m/d/yyyy"}
    }
  ]
}
